From a4fa222ea2d847ace2e8460b1c7b53241a020de7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:04:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/18] nemotron: Super verifies windows of up to 32 rows on
 CUDA (31 MTP drafts a round)

state.max_rows is 32 and state.windowRows(c) the width a checkpoint takes: 32 for a latent MoE (ModelOpt's FP8 lane
tiles of 16 and 32 rows, bf16 and NVFP4 lanes, and per-pair experts give a row the same bits at any width), 16 for every
other one, whose MLX affine-4 decode products (Nano's ModelOpt MTP head among them) tile 16 rows. Window buffers, the
Mamba replay planes, captured windows and head levels, the cost table, the depth rule, copied chains, grammar windows,
the lane facts and the pinned layouts follow it; the latent shared-expert plans cover max_rows, the non-latent ones
stay at 16 rows. --mtp-drafts takes up to max_chain (31), and a lone stream's cap stops at its checkpoint's window.
